Rule 1 says add to .gitignore if it matches common ignore patterns.
- `.pyc`, `.class`, etc. -> No.
- `node_modules/` -> No.
- Editor/IDE -> No.
- System/Env -> No.
- Other common ignores -> `*.log`, coverage...
- Compressed -> No.

Is `package-lock.json` an ignore? Usually NO. It is a source-of-truth file for dependencies and should be committed.
Is `main.py.orig` an ignore? Yes, `.orig` files are backups generated by merge tools or editors and are typically ignored.

So only `*.orig` needs to be added.

